NEARS-1863 — DATA DoR GAP: neither campaign rail has renderable data in multi_food_db.
Blocks the live-render half of QA scenarios 1-3 (item rail renders / banner rail unchanged /
both rails render DIFFERENT content simultaneously). NOT a defect in this change.
Read-only queries only — no DML, nothing seeded to manufacture a pass.

--- item-campaign rail (fed by _getItemCampaignList, the builder this ticket re-rooted) ---
mysql> SELECT COUNT(*) AS item_campaign_rows FROM item_campaigns;
item_campaign_rows
0

  => the table is EMPTY platform-wide. No zone, module or account can render this rail.

--- basic/banner rail (fed by _getBasicCampaignList) ---
mysql> SELECT id,title,status,module_id FROM campaigns;
id  title                        status  module_id
1   QA Single-Store Campaign A   1       1
2   QA Single-Store Campaign B   1       1

mysql> SELECT * FROM campaign_store LIMIT 5;
campaign_id  store_id  campaign_status
1            21        confirmed

mysql> SELECT id,name,zone_id,module_id,status FROM stores WHERE id=21;
id  name         zone_id  module_id  status
21  Fast Market  2        1          0

  => the only linked store is zone 2 AND status=0 (inactive); the app under test runs in
     zone 1, so the banner rail is empty here too.

--- confirmed against the live API (both return an empty list) ---
$ curl -s -H "zoneId: [1]" -H "moduleId: 1" -H "latitude: 23.8103" -H "longitude: 90.4125" \
       http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/campaigns/item
[]
$ curl -s -H "zoneId: [1]" -H "moduleId: 1" -H "latitude: 23.8103" -H "longitude: 90.4125" \
       http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/campaigns/basic
[]

Consequence: the endpoints are provably fetched independently and return 200 (see
campaign-endpoint-independence.log), but no rail CONTENT can be shown on screen, so the
"banners must never appear inside the item rail" proxy cannot be exercised visually.
Fix = a seeder adding >=1 active item_campaign + >=1 basic campaign on an ACTIVE store in
zone 1. Versioned seeder/migration only, per the read-only DB rule.
